id: OBI:0200166
name: data transformation objective
def: "An objective specification to transformation input data into output data" []
is_a: IAO:0000005 ! objective specification

[Term]
id: OBI:0200171
name: partitioning data transformation
def: "A partitioning data transformation is a data transformation that has objective partitioning." []
is_a: OBI:0200000 ! data transformation
relationship: OBI:0000417 OBI:0200172 ! achieves_planned_objective partitioning objective

[Term]
id: OBI:0200172
name: partitioning objective
def: "A partitioning objective is a data transformation objective where the aim is to generate a collection of disjoint non-empty subsets whose union equals a non-empty input set." []
is_a: OBI:0200166 ! data transformation objective

[Term]
id: OBI:0200175
name: class discovery data transformation
def: "A class discovery data transformation (sometimes called unsupervised classification) is a data transformation that has objective class discovery." []
is_a: OBI:0200000 ! data transformation

[Term]
id: OBI:0200178
name: class discovery objective
def: "A class discovery objective (sometimes called unsupervised classification) is a data transformation objective where the aim is to organize input data  (typically vectors of attributes) into classes, where the number of classes and their specifications are not known a priori. Depending on usage, the class assignment can be definite or probabilistic." []
is_a: OBI:0200166 ! data transformation objective

[Term]
id: OBI:0200179
name: class prediction objective
def: "A class prediction objective (sometimes called supervised classification) is a data transformation objective where the aim is to create a predictor from training data through a machine learning technique. The training data consist of pairs of objects (typically vectors of attributes) and\nclass labels for these objects. The resulting predictor can be used to attach class labels to any valid novel input object. Depending on usage, the prediction can be definite or probabilistic. A classification is learned from the training data and can then be tested on test data." []
is_a: OBI:0200166 ! data transformation objective

[Term]
id: OBI:0200188
name: cross validation objective
def: "A cross validation objective is a data transformation objective in which the aim is to partition a sample of data into subsets such that the analysis is initially performed on a single subset, while the other subset(s) are retained for subsequent use in confirming and validating the initial analysis." []
is_a: OBI:0200172 ! partitioning objective

[Term]
id: OBI:0200190
name: clustered data visualization
def: "A data visualization which has input of a clustered data set and produces an output of a report graph which is capable of rendering data of this type." []
is_a: OBI:0200111 ! data visualization
relationship: OBI:0000293 OBI:0000648 {all_only="true"} ! has specified input clustered data set

[Term]
id: OBI:0500000
name: study design
def: "A plan specification comprised of protocols (which may specify how and what kinds of data will be gathered) that are executed as part of an investigation and is realized during a study design execution." []
is_a: IAO:0000104 ! plan specification
relationship: BFO:0000051 OBI:0000272 ! has part protocol

[Term]
id: PATO:0000001
name: quality
namespace: quality
def: "A dependent entity that inheres in a bearer by virtue of how the bearer is related to other entities" [PATOC:GVG]
is_a: BFO:0000020 ! specifically dependent continuant

[Term]
id: PATO:0000033
name: concentration of
namespace: quality
def: "A quality inhering in a substance by virtue of the amount of the bearer's there is mixed with another substance." [Wikipedia:http\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/concentration]
synonym: "concentration" EXACT []
is_a: PATO:0000070 ! amount

[Term]
id: PATO:0000051
name: morphology
namespace: quality
def: "A quality of a single physical entity inhering in the bearer by virtue of the bearer's size or shape or structure." [PATOC:GVG]
is_a: PATO:0001241 ! physical object quality

[Term]
id: PATO:0000070
name: amount
namespace: quality
def: "The number of entities of this type that are part of the whole organism." [PATOC:GVG]
comment: This term was originally named "presence". It has been renamed to reduce ambiguity. Consider annotating with the reciprocal relation,PATO:0001555, has_number_of. For example, rather than E=fin ray Q=count in organism C=10, say E=organism Q=has number of E2= fin ray C=10.
synonym: "count in organism" RELATED []
synonym: "number" RELATED []
synonym: "presence" RELATED []
synonym: "presence or absence in organism" EXACT []
synonym: "quantitative" EXACT []
is_a: PATO:0103000 ! quantitative
relationship: RO:0015012 PATO:0001555 ! reciprocal of has number of

[Term]
id: PATO:0000141
name: structure
namespace: quality
def: "A morphology quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's relative position, shape, arrangements and connectivity of an organism's various parts; the pattern underlying its form." [PATOC:GVG]
synonym: "conformation" BROAD [VT:1000738]
synonym: "relational structural quality" EXACT []
is_a: PATO:0000051 ! morphology

[Term]
id: PATO:0001241
name: physical object quality
namespace: quality
def: "A quality which inheres in a continuant." [PATOC:GVG]
comment: Relational qualities are qualities that hold between multiple entities. Normal (monadic) qualities such as the shape of a eyeball exist purely as a quality of that eyeball. A relational quality such as sensitivity to light is a quality of that eyeball (and connecting nervous system) as it relates to incoming light waves/particles.
synonym: "monadic quality of a continuant" EXACT []
synonym: "monadic quality of an object" NARROW []
synonym: "monadic quality of continuant" NARROW []
synonym: "multiply inhering quality of a physical entity" EXACT []
synonym: "quality of a continuant" EXACT []
synonym: "quality of a single physical entity" EXACT []
synonym: "quality of an object" EXACT []
synonym: "quality of continuant" EXACT []
xref: snap:Quality
is_a: BFO:0000019 ! quality
is_a: PATO:0000001 ! quality

[Term]
id: PATO:0001555
name: has number of
namespace: quality
def: "The number of parts of a particular type that the bearer entity has. This is a relational quality, and thus holds between two entities: the bearer of the quality, and the type of parts." [PATOC:CJM]
synonym: "cardinality" RELATED []
synonym: "extra or missing physical or functional parts" EXACT []
synonym: "has or lacks parts of type" EXACT []
synonym: "mereological quality" EXACT []
synonym: "number" RELATED []
synonym: "number of" EXACT []
xref: OBO_REL:has_part
is_a: PATO:0000070 ! amount

[Term]
id: PATO:0001842
name: acidity
namespace: quality
def: "A concentration quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing acid (hydrogen ions)." [biology-online:biology-online]
synonym: "pH" EXACT []
is_a: PATO:0000033 ! concentration of

[Term]
id: PATO:0010001
name: disconnected
namespace: quality
def: "A structural quality inhering in the bearer by virtue of the bearer consisting of multiple structures lacking any physical connection to each other." [GOC:dos]
is_a: PATO:0000141 ! structure
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172

[Term]
id: PATO:0103000
name: quantitative
namespace: quality
def: "A quality of an entity that can be represented numerically, including anything that can be counted, measured, or given a numerical value." [https://libguides.macalester.edu/c.php?g=527786&p=3608639, https://www.nnlm.gov/guides/data-glossary/quantitative-data]
is_a: PATO:0000001 ! quality

[Term]
id: PR:000000001
is_a: CHEBI:33695 ! information biomacromolecule

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000000
name: process rate metric
def: "A key process metric that represents a quantitative metric, describing rates or fluxes associated, for instance, wiht growth, product formation, substrate consumption, or respiration, during a fermentation process." []
synonym: "key precision fermentation process rate metric" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000078 ! key process metric

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000002
name: fermentation project
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A precision fermentation process that consist of a single fermentation experiment or multiple related experiments." []
synonym: "project" EXACT []
is_a: OBI:0000066 ! investigation
is_a: PREFER:9000003 ! precision fermentation process

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000003
name: fermentation experiment
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A precision fermentation process that consists of sets of fermentation runs conducted within the same project, all following a shared experimental approach or protocol." []
synonym: "experiment" EXACT []
is_a: OBI:0000070 ! assay
is_a: PREFER:9000003 ! precision fermentation process
relationship: BFO:0000050 PREFER:0000002 ! part of fermentation project

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000004
name: fermentation run
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A precision fermentation process that is carried out under defined experimental conditions (e.g., temperature, pH, agitation) using a single bioreactor system." []
synonym: "cell culture process" BROAD []
xref: CHMO:0001624
is_a: PREFER:9000003 ! precision fermentation process
relationship: BFO:0000050 PREFER:0000003 ! part of fermentation experiment
relationship: PREFER:8000006 PREFER:0000014 ! uses bioreactor bioreactor
relationship: PREFER:8000011 PREFER:0000008 ! has cultivation condition cultivation condition
relationship: PREFER:8000015 PREFER:0000012 ! cultures cell cell biocatalyst
relationship: PREFER:8000016 PREFER:0000018 ! has collected offline sample
relationship: PREFER:8000017 CHEBI:24431 ! has measured compound chemical entity
relationship: RO:0000057 PREFER:0000011 ! has participant fermentation medium

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000005
name: alkaline cultivation condition
def: "A cultivation condition that represents the alkalinity related aspects of a fermentation cultivation process, grouping process control varibales and process measurement variables that describe or regulate the pH and buffering state of the cultivation environment." []
is_a: PREFER:0000008 ! cultivation condition

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000006
name: gravimetric feed rate control variable
def: "A process control variable that represents the target rate at which the feed (based on its weight) is added to a bioreactor or fermentation system during a fermentation process." []
is_a: PREFER:0000009 ! feed control variable
relationship: OBI:0001938 uom:g.h-1 ! has value specification gram per hour
relationship: PREFER:8000020 PREFER:0000075 ! setpoint of gravimetric feed rate measurement variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000007
name: temperature cultivation condition
def: "A cultivation condition that represents the temperature related aspects of a fermentation cultivation process, grouping process control varibales and process measurement variables that describe or regulate the thermal state of the cultivation environment." []
is_a: PREFER:0000008 ! cultivation condition

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000008
name: cultivation condition
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "An information content entity that represents a set of process conditions, grouping relevant process control variables and process measurement variables, describing the environmental and physicochemical conditions under which cells are cultivated." []
synonym: "fermentation culture condition" EXACT []
xref: EDAM:3724
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity
relationship: BFO:0000051 PREFER:0000015 ! has part operational parameter

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000009
name: feed control variable
def: "A precision fermentation process control variable that defines the feed control of a bioreactor or fermentation system during the fermentation process." []
synonym: "precision fermentation process feed control variable" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000037 ! feed medium cultivation condition
is_a: PREFER:9000000 ! precision fermentation process control variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000010
name: fermentation culture
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A material entity consisting of a cell population that is cultivated under controlled environmental conditions supporting a fermentation process." []
comment: Fermentation cultures are used in bioprocesses for various applications including precision fermentation, bioremediation, and production of biofuels and pharmaceuticals.
synonym: "cultured cell population" NARROW [OBI:0100060]
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity
relationship: PREFER:8000010 PREFER:0000200 ! has fermentation culture type fermentation culture role

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000011
name: fermentation medium
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A material entity consisting of an aqueous mixture of macronutrients, micronturients, and buffering agents that is used to support cell growth, metabolic activity and product formation during a fermentation process." []
synonym: "cultivation medium" EXACT []
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity
relationship: PREFER:8000004 CHEBI:24431 ! has medium ingredient chemical entity

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000012
name: cell biocatalyst
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A material entity consisting of a whole living cell that is used as a catalyst for bioproduction, catalyzing a biochemical reaction or transformation through their intrinsec or genetically modified metabolic activity." []
comment: In a biotransformation process or bioprocess, a cell biocatalyst converts substrates (organic or inorganic compounds) into outputs such as products, by-products, and cell biomass. Energy derived from substrate conversion is used for product formation, growth and cellular maintenance.
synonym: "biocatalyst" BROAD []
synonym: "biological catalyst" BROAD []
synonym: "catalyst" BROAD []
synonym: "cell catalyst" EXACT []
synonym: "cell factory" EXACT []
synonym: "microbial cell factory" NARROW []
synonym: "WCB" EXACT OMO:0003012 [DOI: 10.1201/9781003413134]
synonym: "whole-cell biocatalyst" EXACT [DOI: 10.1186/s12934-017-0724-7]
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000013
name: taxon quality
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A quality of one or more biological organisms, as well as of parts of organism pertaining to a biological taxon." [PMID:18586729]
synonym: "taxon" BROAD [NCBITaxon:1]
xref: http://purl.org/biotop/btl2.owl#TaxonQuality
is_a: BFO:0000019 ! quality

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000014
name: bioreactor
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A device or system that is a material entity designed to support the run of a biological and biochemical process by controlling regulated environmental and cultivation conditions, such as temperature, agitation or nutrient injection at different scales, including lab-scale, pilot plant, and industrial-scale systems." [OBI:0001046]
comment: While this term is equivalent to OBI:0001046, PREFER has specific modelling that makes it more difficult to maintain if used directly. A decision was hence made to create this new term in PREFER and map it to OBI:0001046 instead.
synonym: "bioreactor system" EXACT []
synonym: "fermenter" NARROW [MSIO:0000167]
xref: OBI:0001046
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity
relationship: PREFER:8000008 PREFER:0000185 ! has bioreactor scale bioreactor scale
relationship: PREFER:8000018 PREFER:0000180 ! has operational mode operation mode control variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000015
name: operational parameter
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "An information content entity that represents a set of configurable settings used to operate and control a fermentation process, grouping process control variables and mode dependent parameters that define how cultivation conditions are regulated in a bioreactor or fermentation system during the process." []
comment: Operational parameters may vary depending on the selected fermentation operational mode (e.g. batch, fed-batch, continuous) and are realized through instrument or system configuration.
synonym: "operational setting" BROAD []
synonym: "parameter" BROAD [NCIT:C44175]
xref: REPR:InstrumentSetting
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000016
name: fermentation phase
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A time interval of a fermentation process." []
is_a: PREFER:9000003 ! precision fermentation process
relationship: BFO:0000050 PREFER:0000004 ! part of fermentation run

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000017
name: phase event
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "An operational intervention set by user that triggers the start or end of the fermentation phase." []
is_a: PREFER:9000003 ! precision fermentation process

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000018
name: offline sample
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A material entity consisting of a sample that has been withdrawn from a bioprocess system or bioreactor at a specific time point during the ongoing fermentation run for subsequent offline analysis of various compounds, such as substrates, products, and by-products, and biomass." []
synonym: "collected sample" EXACT []
synonym: "material sample" BROAD [OBI:0000747]
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000019
name: temperature setpoint control variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A precision fermentation process control variable that represents the target temperature value to be regulated and maintained within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a fermentation process." []
synonym: "precision fermentation process temperature setpoint control variable" EXACT []
synonym: "target temperature" EXACT []
synonym: "target temperature value" EXACT []
synonym: "target Tº" EXACT []
synonym: "temperature control setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "temperature reference point" EXACT []
synonym: "temperature reference value" EXACT []
synonym: "temperature setting" EXACT [AFO_/result#AFR:0001255]
synonym: "Tº setpoint" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000007 ! temperature cultivation condition
is_a: PREFER:0000015 ! operational parameter
is_a: PREFER:9000000 ! precision fermentation process control variable
relationship: OBI:0001938 PREFER:9000004 ! has value specification unit
relationship: PREFER:8000020 PREFER:0000041 ! setpoint of temperature measurement variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000020
name: pH setpoint control variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A precision fermentation process control variable that represents the target pH value to be regulated and maintained within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a fermentation process." []
synonym: "pH control setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "ph control setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "ph setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "precision fermentation process pH setpoint control variable" EXACT []
synonym: "target pH" EXACT []
synonym: "target ph" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000005 ! alkaline cultivation condition
is_a: PREFER:0000015 ! operational parameter
is_a: PREFER:9000000 ! precision fermentation process control variable
relationship: OBI:0001938 uom:%5BpH%5D ! has value specification pH based unit
relationship: PREFER:8000020 PREFER:0000040 ! setpoint of pH measurement variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000021
name: pH base solution
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A liquid material entity with basic (alkaline) properties that is used to increase the pH of a solution or system.\n\nIn a fermentation process, it is added manually or automatically to the fermentation run to control and maintain the pH at the defined setpoint or desired value." []
synonym: "pH control base solution" EXACT []
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000022
name: pH acid solution
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A liquid material entity with acidic properties that is used to decrease the pH of a solution or system.\n\nIn a fermentation process, it is added manually or automatically to the fermentation run to control and maintain the pH at the defined setpoint or desired value." []
synonym: "pH control acid solution" EXACT []
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000023
name: core balance metric
def: "A precision fermentation process calculated variable that represents a quantitative metric derived from balance calculations over a process, used to characterize the balance of inputs and outputs within a bioreactor or fermenter system during the fermentation process." []
synonym: "elemental balance metric" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:9000002 ! precision fermentation process calculated variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000024
name: fermentation medium cultivation condition
def: "A cultivation condition that represents the fermentation medium related aspects of a fermentation cultivation process, grouping process control varibales and process measurement variables that describe or regulate the state of the fermentation medium within the cultivation environment." []
is_a: PREFER:0000008 ! cultivation condition

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000025
name: dissolved oxygen setpoint control variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A precision fermentation process dissolved oxygen control variable that represents the target dissolved oxygen value to be regulated and maintained within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a fermentation process." []
synonym: "dissolved oxygen setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "DO setpoint" EXACT OMO:0003012 []
synonym: "precision fermentation process dissolved oxygen setpoint control variable" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000015 ! operational parameter
is_a: PREFER:0000119 ! dissolved oxygen control variable
relationship: OBI:0001938 uom:%25 ! has value specification percent
relationship: PREFER:8000020 PREFER:0000039 ! setpoint of dissolved oxygen measurement variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000026
name: dissolved oxygen cascade level control variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A precision fermentation process dissolved oxygen control variable that represents the cascade control system linked to a parameter to achieve the desired dissolved oxygen level within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a fermentation process." []
comment: For instance, in fed-batch operation mode there could be three different cascade levels. Level 1 involves adjusting the stirrer speed parameter. Level 2 involves adjusting the air flow parameter. Level 3 involves adjusting the oxygen flow parameter.
synonym: "dissolved oxygen control strategy variable" EXACT []
synonym: "DO cascade level control variable" EXACT []
synonym: "precision fermentation process dissolved oxygen cascade level control variable" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000015 ! operational parameter
is_a: PREFER:0000119 ! dissolved oxygen control variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000027
name: maximum stirring setpoint control variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A precision fermentation process dissolved oxygen control variable that represents the target maximum revolutions per minute (rpm) of the bioreactor stirrer to be regulated and or maintained within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a fermentation process." []
synonym: "maximum shaking speed setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "maximum shaking speed setpoint control variable" EXACT []
synonym: "maximum stirring speed setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "precision fermentation process maximum stirring setpoint control variable" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000015 ! operational parameter
is_a: PREFER:0000119 ! dissolved oxygen control variable
relationship: OBI:0001938 PREFER:7000008 ! has value specification revolution per minute
relationship: PREFER:8000020 PREFER:0000054 ! setpoint of stirrer speed measurement variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000028
name: minimum stirring setpoint control variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A precision fermentation process dissolved oxygen control variable that represents the target minimum revolutions per minute (rpm) of the bioreactor stirrer to be regulated and or maintained within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a fermentation process." []
synonym: "minimum shaking speed setpoin" EXACT []
synonym: "minimum shaking speed setpoint control variable" EXACT []
synonym: "minimum stirring speed setpoin" EXACT []
synonym: "minimum stirring speed setpoint control variable" EXACT []
