[Term]
id: PREFER:0000063
name: oxygen transfer rate variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A respiratory rate metric variable that represents the rate at which oxygen is transferred from the gas phase or fermenter air into the liquid phase within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a fermentation process." []
comment: Physical gas transfer. Dynamic respiratory metric
synonym: "OTR variable" EXACT OMO:0003012 []
is_a: PREFER:0000158 ! respiratory rate metric
relationship: OBI:0001938 uom:mol.h-1 ! has value specification mole per hour

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000064
name: carbon dioxide transfer rate variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A respiratory rate metric that represents the rate at which carbon dioxide is transferred out of the bioreactor or fermentation system during a fermentation process." []
comment: Physical gas transfer. Dynamic respiratory metric. Important as carbon dioxide is considered a by-product in aerobic processes, and so is a parameter used for predicting biomass concentration, evaluating energetic efficiencies of growth, monitoring growth yields and controlling fed batch processes like airflow rates or stir speeds.
synonym: "CTR variable" EXACT OMO:0003012 []
is_a: PREFER:0000158 ! respiratory rate metric
relationship: OBI:0001938 uom:mol.h-1 ! has value specification mole per hour

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000065
