[Term]
id: PREFER:0000085
name: microbioreactor scale
def: "A laboratory bioreactor scale that refers to very small volume bioreactor systems designed for high-throughput screening, typically operated at working volumes in the range of approximately a few microliters." []
comment: For instance, microtiter plates (MTPs) fall within this category.
is_a: PREFER:0000186 ! laboratory bioreactor scale

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000086
name: minibioreactor scale
def: "A laboratory bioreactor scale that refers to small volume bioreactor systems designed for parallelized process development and experimentation, typically operated at working volumes in the range of approximately 10 milliliters to a few liters." []
comment: For instance, Ambr250 or Pioreactors fall within this category.
is_a: PREFER:0000186 ! laboratory bioreactor scale

